<h1>Advocates of Honor</h1>
<p><i>The Advocates of Honor's own page, kept as the clan wrote it.</i>
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Mission_Statement">Mission Statement</span></h2>
<p>The Advocates of Honor are a group of friends, bound together by their legendary leaders, and a driving sense of duty and loyalty to Valhalla. They live within the rules of the game, but more, are bound tightly by their own sense of honor, and the morals that have been passed down from their clan lords. The clan stands as a whole, more powerful than any of the individual pieces that make it up, and it will always be so. The Advocates are known throughout the land for their passionate support of one another. It is with extreme peril that even the lowliest Advocate should be offended in any way.
</p><p>The mission, of the Advocates of Honor, is to bring a new sense of pride and strength to the citizens of Valhalla. The leaders of AoH have long been known as the movers and shakers of Valhalla. You have seen their members as builders, as questers, and as leaders. For players at any level of the game, the way to immortality, and previously unknown power, is through the Advocates of Honor.
</p><p>Such prestige does not come without sacrifice. Advocates are expected to keep the moral high-ground in all things. They are well known to excommunicate members at the slightest question of worthiness. They demand 100% loyalty, and absolute support for all other members, in all things.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Criteria_for_Membership">Criteria for Membership</span></h2>
<p>Advocates will be accepted on individual merits, as they fit the clans need. The clan will always come before any of its members.
</p><p>There are numerous disparate routes to gain entry into the Advocates, and we will not attempt to limit them in this document. We will state, that the reputation of any member will be a key factor in their consideration. The ability to offer a unique set of characteristics or abilities, or specialty in a specific part of the mud, will certainly be advantageous to any perspective members.
</p><p>The Advocates seek trustworthy members, who have proven their commitment and desire to bring improvements to Valhalla and its atmosphere. Documented efforts may be referenced in order to bring a boon to application of any potential members.
</p><p>Generally approved of, but not required, characteristics include:
</p>
<ul><li>Over one year play time (RL).</li>
<li>A character with greater than 2000 levels.</li>
<li>Extreme proficiency in any particular role or path.</li>
<li>Verifiable Admin-granted positions (Builder, Guide, Valhalla Times Reporter)</li>
<li>All existing members of AoH needs to agree on new members by voting.</li>
<li>Higher skills and knowledge about PK</li></ul>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Clan_Rules">Clan Rules</span></h2>
<p>The Advocates of Honor stand by their own sense of what is right and honorable, more handily than any written set of rules. Again, we will not attempt to limit the scope of these clan rules by individually listing items. Instead, it is the ideas listed here, and in other founding documents, that the Lords of Honor will make their judgments by.
</p><p>It goes without saying, that all members will be required to follow all written rules of Valhalla. More than that however, members must stand for the betterment of the mud. Anyone seen has being a detriment to the clan, or the mud, will be subject to immediate termination of membership privileges.
</p><p>Advocates are made as members for life. Members are required to join all characters they are associated with to the clan. All members are expected to put the good of the clan before themselves, or any individual. Anyone who voluntarily disassociates themselves from AoH will be subject to disciplinary action, ad infinium.
</p><p><br />
